Certificates for the finite-prime Weil matrices of Sections 17.9-17.10 of Riemann_Hypothesis_Li_and_Monotonicity.md.

CHECKED (exact integer arithmetic, kernel evaluation; no axioms):
  * for each Davenport-Heilbronn window: a vector x with x^T A x < 0 that survives rounding every entry of A by one unit
    of 10^-30, and the inertia of A (no vanishing leading minor, number of sign changes in 1, D_1, ..., D_m);
  * for the zeta window: A - lambda I has all leading principal minors positive (Sylvester), i.e. A >= lambda I.

NOT CHECKED: that the integers are the true Weil quadratic forms.  They are 50-digit numerical output (prime sums and
quadrature for the archimedean term), compared with the zero side outside Lean (agreement 1e-13 to 1e-24).  The Jacobi/
Sylvester theorems that turn minors into inertia are classical and are not formalised here.
-/

abbrev Mat := List (List Int)

def dot (u v : List Int) : Int := (List.zipWith (· * ·) u v).foldl (· + ·) 0
def mulVec (A : Mat) (x : List Int) : List Int := A.map (fun r => dot r x)
def quad (A : Mat) (x : List Int) : Int := dot x (mulVec A x)
def l1 (x : List Int) : Int := x.foldl (fun s v => s + Int.ofNat v.natAbs) 0

def minors (M : Mat) : List Int := Id.run do
  let n := M.length
  let mut a : Array (Array Int) := (M.map List.toArray).toArray
  let mut prev : Int := 1
  let mut out : Array Int := #[]
  for k in [0:n] do
    let piv := a[k]![k]!
    out := out.push piv
    for i in [k+1:n] do
      let mut row := a[i]!
      for j in [k+1:n] do
        row := row.set! j ((a[i]![j]! * piv - a[i]![k]! * a[k]![j]!) / prev)
      a := a.set! i row
    prev := piv
  return out.toList

def signChanges : List Int → Nat
  | a :: b :: rest => (if (a > 0 && b < 0) || (a < 0 && b > 0) then 1 else 0) + signChanges (b :: rest)
  | _ => 0

